# Files git should never diff, merge or line-ending-normalise.
# cursors/ alone is ~92 MB of .cur/.ani; letting git attempt a text diff on
# those makes `git status` and GitHub's diff view unusable.
*.exe   binary
*.bin   binary
*.cur   binary
*.ani   binary
*.ico   binary
*.png   binary

# PowerShell scripts must stay byte-exact: install.ps1 and make_release.ps1 are
# UTF-8 *with BOM* and Windows PowerShell 5.1 mis-decodes them without it, which
# shows up as "表达式或语句中包含意外的标记 }" at parse time. -text tells git to
# keep the line endings it finds instead of normalising them.
*.ps1   -text
*.bat   -text

# Everything else: no global convention is imposed, because the whole tree is
# already committed with CRLF and core.autocrlf=false on the maintainer's
# machine. Switching to `* text=auto` would rewrite the index for ~100 files.
